From 5f820ae4fc20b1ff4c199657f78828efc295fc56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:00:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Rebuild cmocka.keyring from the key upstream publishes at
https://cryptomilk.org/0x8DFF53E18F2ABC8D8F3C92237EE0FC4DCC014E3D_asn_cryptomilk_org_gpgkey.asc,
completed from keyservers/WKD with the older self-signatures and subkey
bindings the release needs (same certificate(s)).
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
